course: dictionary
lesson: 1971
title: Complementary: going well together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Complementary means two things that go well together, so that each one makes the other better or more complete. «Colour chains need two steps: first work out what a mix makes, then use the colour wheel, where opposite colours are complementary.» Here the clue is the colour wheel: complementary colours are the pairs that sit opposite each other on it.
explain: The same word works in maths. In maths, if one angle is 30°, its complementary angle is 60°, because the two add up to 90°. Ask yourself what would fit: if two things complete each other, complementary fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Complementary colours are opposite each other on the colour wheel, like orange and blue or red and green; side by side they make each other look stronger.» Put "matching" in place of complementary and it still makes sense, but the sentence adds that each colour makes the other look stronger.
fact: Complementary means going well together and making each other better or complete.
fact: In maths, complementary angles add up to 90 degrees.
fact: In art, complementary colours sit opposite each other on the colour wheel, like red and green.
fact: Complementary colours make each other stand out, but mixing them gives a muddy brown or grey.
fact: «Complementary medicine» is treatment used alongside normal medicine.
exercise: «Complementary colours are opposite each other on the colour wheel, like orange and blue or red and green.» Which pair is complementary? | *Red and green | Red and red | Red and yellow
exercise: In maths, if one angle is 30°, what is its complementary angle? | *60° | 180° | 30° | 150°
exercise: Two friends with complementary skills make a good team. What does complementary mean here? | Working apart and never meeting | *Going well together and making each other better | Exactly the same as each other
test: Mixing complementary colours gives what? | Pure white | *A muddy brown or grey | A clear, bright green
test: Complementary angles add up to how many degrees? | 180 | 45 | 360 | *90
exam: Which word means going well together and making each other better or complete? | Glum | Curt | *Complementary | Treacherous
